---
description: Keep engineering work small, targeted, and verified
alwaysApply: true
---

# Token-efficient engineering

- Search for relevant symbols before opening large files.
- Read only the context required for the current task.
- Trace affected callers before changing an interface.
- Prefer the smallest complete change.
- Reuse existing project patterns and dependencies.
- Avoid unrelated refactoring and repeated full-project scans.
- Run focused tests before broader test suites when appropriate.
- Verify the final Git diff.
- Never claim tests passed without executing them.
- Never reveal secrets or credentials.
- Summarize changed files, verification results and remaining risks.
